<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jibla</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Dhu Jibla</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jibla, also called Dhu Jibla, is a town in the highlands of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yemen">Yemen</a>, south of Ibb. Around 1087 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arwa-al-sulayhi">Queen Arwa</a> al-Sulayhi made it the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sulayhid-dynasty">Sulayhid dynasty</a>, building a palace and the great mosque that holds her tomb. After her death it passed to the Zurayids of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aden">Aden</a> and later to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubids</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jibla.jpg" alt="Jibla" width="320" height="200" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rod Waddington · CC BY-SA 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Yemen_-_49222204591.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
